<ServiceLayout title="Massage Therapy" description="Therapeutic massage therapy at Frey Clinic of Chiropractic in Napoleon, OH to relieve tension, improve circulation, and complement chiropractic care." heroImage="/images/hero-massage.jpg" heroAlt="Professional massage therapy session">

<p>
  Massage therapy is a powerful complement to chiropractic adjustments. By addressing the soft tissues — muscles, tendons, and fascia — massage helps prepare the body for adjustment, extends the benefits of treatment, and provides relief on its own.
</p>

<hr class="rule rule--accent" style="margin-block:var(--sp-6);" />

<h2>Benefits of massage therapy</h2>
<ul style="list-style:disc; padding-left:var(--sp-5); margin-bottom:var(--sp-5);">
  <li style="margin-bottom:var(--sp-2);">Reduced muscle tension and pain</li>
  <li style="margin-bottom:var(--sp-2);">Improved blood circulation</li>
  <li style="margin-bottom:var(--sp-2);">Enhanced flexibility and range of motion</li>
  <li style="margin-bottom:var(--sp-2);">Stress reduction</li>
  <li style="margin-bottom:var(--sp-2);">Better sleep quality</li>
  <li style="margin-bottom:var(--sp-2);">Faster recovery from injuries</li>
</ul>

<h2>How it works with chiropractic</h2>
<p>
  When muscles are tight or in spasm, they can pull vertebrae out of alignment. Massage therapy relaxes these muscles, making chiropractic adjustments more effective and longer-lasting. Together, the two approaches address both the skeletal and muscular components of pain and dysfunction.
</p>

</ServiceLayout>
